A||N||8||Seanh||How hard is it to install scoops?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||04-01-2001||01:50 AM||||I was wondering. I am pretty good with engine work, but I have never worked with autobody before. I want a vent behind the radiator, that sets down into the hood. And also a rear faceing scoop over the engine compartment. How hard is it really to do this? Is it somthing I should try, or just take it in the pocket book and let a body shop do it? I will definatly have a shop repaint the parts, but wondering if I should try cutting and glassing myself? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||04-01-2001||02:31 AM|||| The hood is a SOB to do yourself but a decklid scoop is very easy.If your car is a GT its real easy.Measure, drill,test fit,cut the hole, bolt on and you're done. A little more work is involved with a coupe(cutting the hump off, but still is not that bad. I did mine in about 4 hours.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||04-01-2001||02:43 AM||||when i tried to vent my hood i got a spare one and cut the vents into it. it came out ok so i just swaped hoods. i've been a little araid of trying to glass them in, but even if i messed it up (i kinda think it should be easier than the cutting, but paint some ways off so i'm in no hurry to get it done), i've stll got the original hood.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||04-01-2001||12:39 PM||||Trunk lid scoop info can be found here: <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/dxr" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com/dxr</A> <P>It's just a job you have to jump into. Once you start you'll see how easy it is. Shop labor rate = $60.00 per hr.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=11236669&p=39158346&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>A local shop wanted $600.00 to finish and paint this set of side scoops!! I did it myself, it took about 3 weeks<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=12120996&p=43938685&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=12120996&p=43932249&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
